          <attvalue for="35" value="0.7" />
          <attvalue for="36" value="Sustained increases in global crude prices create domestic economic and political pressure (industry, consumers, allied partners) that push the executive toward more permissive or conciliatory policy moves to restore supplies and lower prices." />
